#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""blockads-fw: the root helper of blockads-linux.

Applies, verifies and reverts the iptables rules that send local DNS traffic
to the blockadsd socket, and edits /etc/blockads-linux/firewall.conf.

    blockads-fw apply [--verify]       (ExecStartPost)
    blockads-fw revert [--all-backends] (ExecStartPre, ExecStop, ExecStopPost, failsafe)
    blockads-fw status [--json]
    blockads-fw doctor [--json]
    blockads-fw set-config             (pkexec; JSON object on stdin)

Rules:
- stdlib only, one file, no shell: every command is an argv list with a timeout;
- binaries come from /usr/sbin or /usr/bin, and every component of their real
  path must be root-owned and not group/world-writable;
- never read anything the 'blockads' user can write;
- never persist rules; revert never stops early.

Exit status: 0 success, 1 failure (apply reverted, or something was left
behind by revert), 2 invalid configuration or usage.
"""

